(3596726, 501340, 57229, '<td valign="top">Steve Davidson is right on the money as far as I''m concerned. For the idea, concept and set-up this is worth all the votes in the world, but then it doesn''t quite make it as a photograph. I think a darker (and preferably non-reflective?) background might have helped, to set off and contrast with the chrome and stainless steel - where light''s reflected off the corkscrew it''s the same colour and tone as the background material.<br/> <br/>It''s too good for 5.6, in many ways, but I can''t say it''s wrong. Really enjoyed the picture though.</td>', 'Steve Davidson is right on the money as far as I''m concerned. For the idea, concept and set-up this is worth all the votes in the world, but then it doesn''t quite make it as a photograph. I think a darker (and preferably non-reflective?) background might have helped, to set off and contrast with the chrome and stainless steel - where light''s reflected off the corkscrew it''s the same colour and tone as the background material. It''s too good for 5.6, in many ways, but I can''t say it''s wrong. Really enjoyed the picture though.', '2007-04-30 17:35:55.000000', NULL, 0),
